## Light No Fire at a glance

Light No Fire is the next game from Hello Games, the studio behind No Man's Sky. It is a fantasy adventure about exploring, building and surviving together on a procedurally generated planet that Hello Games says is the size of Earth. The game has an official Steam listing, but when we checked on 26 November 2026, its release date still read **To be announced**.

## What we know so far

- **Developer and publisher:** Hello Games.
- **Release date:** none announced. Steam says "To be announced", so this article doesn't give a year or quarter.
- **Platforms:** the Steam listing is for Windows. It is the only platform we could confirm.
- **Play modes:** Steam lists single-player, multiplayer and online co-op.
- **Trailer:** the official announcement trailer is on the Steam page and on the official site, lightnofire.com.
- **Languages:** English with full audio, plus French, Italian, German, Spanish, Russian, and Simplified and Traditional Chinese, according to Steam.

## What Hello Games has described

The official description splits the game into four ideas.

**A shared world.** Players from around the world can meet, build persistent buildings and communities, and survive together. You can also head off alone and discover places for others to find later.

**A procedural planet.** The world is open with no boundaries. Hello Games describes a dense planet with varied biomes, its own enemies and resources to gather.

**A fantasy setting.** The studio presents an ancient world full of lore and mystery in which "you're not the hero." It names classic fantasy adventure as the inspiration.

**Exploration at scale.** The description mentions climbing any mountain, sailing oceans and rivers, riding wild beasts and flying dragons. Hello Games calls the game a survival sandbox with the depth of a role-playing game.

## Why there is no date here

Several sites have published guessed release windows for Light No Fire. None of them come from Hello Games. Until the official listing changes from "To be announced", any year you see is speculation, so this article doesn't quote one.

## What's still unconfirmed

- **Release date or window:** not announced.
- **Console versions:** not confirmed on the official pages we checked.
- **System requirements:** Steam lists the operating system as "To be confirmed" and gives no hardware requirements.
- **Price and business model:** Steam shows no price, and the official pages don't say whether there will be ongoing purchases.
- **How multiplayer works in practice:** the official pages don't yet say how many players can share a world or how servers will work.

We have not played Light No Fire. Everything above comes from Hello Games' own descriptions, not from hands-on testing.

## How to follow it

Wishlist the game on Steam or check the official site. When Hello Games announces a date, it should appear on both. If an article quotes a date, check whether it links to one of these pages.

